From: Dian QK <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:35:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Bluetooth: preserve the initial management power transition

Do not clear HCI_AUTO_OFF from the controller setup callback. The HCI core
uses this flag to complete the management power-on transition after setup,
including registering the SMP channels. Clearing it leaves LE connections
without a Security Manager until the adapter is toggled off and on, so
keyboard passkey pairing fails with "security requested but not available".

The existing t880_no_sleep close callback still keeps the physical BGF
powered; the core must retain ownership of its logical power-state flags.

Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/net/bluetooth/hci_sync.c?id=a091755fa00cc93bd01bf1ead191374550eb9b94
---
--- a/connectivity/bt/mt66xx/btmtk_main.c
+++ b/connectivity/bt/mt66xx/btmtk_main.c
@@ -3579,15 +3579,14 @@
 		}
 		/*
 		 * T880: program the nvdata address before the core reads it,
-		 * and stay powered after setup (a BGF power cycle does not come
-		 * back yet; xaga likewise avoids the auto power-off).
+		 * keeping the core management power transition and SMP registration.
+		 * t880_no_sleep keeps the physical BGF powered in bt_close.
 		 */
 		if (btmtk_t880_get_bdaddr(&addr)) {
 			ret = btmtk_t880_set_bdaddr(hdev, &addr);
 			if (ret)
 				return ret;
 		}
-		hci_dev_clear_flag(hdev, HCI_AUTO_OFF);
 		return ret;
 	}
 	return 0;
